  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ECOWAS: Strengthening agri-food trade in the region through institutional coordination and business support</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ECOWAS Agricultural Trade (EAT) programme, funded by the Federal Ministry of Economic Cooperation and Development (BMZ), &amp;quot;One World &amp;ndash; No Hunger&amp;quot; special initiative, is a crucial component of the German-ECOWAS cooperation and implemented by The Deutsche Gesellschaft f&amp;uuml;r Internationale Zusammenarbeit GmbH (GIZ) and The International Trade Centre (ITC). This initiative is designed to tackle regional policy coordination, economic integration and food security, focusing on enhancing intra-ECOWAS agro-food-trade.</narrative>
  </description>
